    "q-161658": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161658",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le y,\\,0\\le x\\le 3-y-z}.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{0}^{3-y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}[x]_{x=0}^{x=3-y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}3-y-z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(3-y)z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3-y)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3y-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
