      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14117154/assets/daedf62c68ba62dee844cf17efc2d767da47a06ceccaedde854779f542b90114.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front and right ones, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14117154/assets/7c1738e97bc16a32f86d6901136afc4d9e288035d170fcd640db340ad36d19c5.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane.\n\nTo find the top boundary curve of $D$ in the form $z=z(y),$ we substitute $x=1$ into the equation $x=2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z:$\n\n$$\n1=2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z\\,⟹\\,z=2-\\frac{2}{3}y\n$$\n\nThen, we have\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-\\frac{2}{3}y},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14117154/assets/ea8b8397163309a11aa478fcc21ab53ee293c19f0d77a93b5c3d3472bb0eba70.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-\\frac{2}{3}y,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3-z/2}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y/3-z/2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}(2-\\frac{y}{3}-\\frac{z}{2})-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}2-\\frac{y}{3}-\\frac{z}{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[(2-\\frac{y}{3})z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2-2y/3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}((2-\\frac{y}{3})(2-\\frac{2y}{3})-\\frac{1}{4}{(2-\\frac{2y}{3})}^{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2-\\frac{2y}{3})((2-\\frac{y}{3})-\\frac{1}{4}(2-\\frac{2y}{3}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2-\\frac{2y}{3})(\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{6})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3-\\frac{4y}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[3y-\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{27}]}_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =(3(3)-\\frac{2(3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{3}^{3}}{27})-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
