    "q-161679": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161679",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane and the plane $z=x+y+2,$ and the planes $x=-1,$ $x=0,$ $y=0,$ $y=1.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le x+y+2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x+y+2}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=x+y+2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x+y+2\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[(x+2)y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x+2+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x+\\frac{5}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}x]}_{x=-1}^{x=0} \\\\  & =0-(\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
