    "q-161717": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161717",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Consider the solid enclosed between the parabolic cylinders $y=-4+{x}^{2}$ and $y=5-{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-3}^{3}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,z)\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+{x}^{2} & =5-{z}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xz$-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,-4+{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 5-{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the circle ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-4+{x}^{2}}^{5-{z}^{2}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-{z}^{2})-(-4+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-3\\le x\\le 3.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =(9-{x}^{2})+(9-{x}^{2})+(9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =27-3{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
