    "q-40319": {
      "dom_id": "step-q40319",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $x=5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=9-4{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9-4{y}^{2} \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le x\\le 9-4{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $9{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}^{9-4{y}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(9-4{y}^{2})-(5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}}}\\,9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}})}^{2}+(9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =(9-9{y}^{2})+(9-9{y}^{2})+(9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =27-27{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
